{"id": "DfM17U6RzLs", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "Is Dhanteras really about buying GOLD? Its other name is Dhanvantari Trayodashi, and the Puranas tell a very different story. 🪔\n\nWhen the gods churned the ocean of milk, they churned for ONE thing: amrit (Bhagavata Purana 8.6). Treasures came up first: Kamadhenu, Airavata, the Kaustubha jewel. Then Lakshmi herself, the goddess of wealth. But the gods kept churning.\n\nLast of all rose Dhanvantari, carrying a jug full of amrit (Bhagavata 8.8.31–35): the god of health, who gave the world Ayurveda (2.7.21).\n\nWealth came first. Life was the prize.\n\nAnd for Dhanteras night, the Padma Purana (Uttara Khanda 122) gives one rule: a lamp for Yama outside your door, so untimely death stays away. Not one word about gold.\n\nSo this Friday: light the Yama diya at dusk, pray to Dhanvantari for your family's health, and buy gold if you like. It's a custom, not the rule. ✨\n\n📚 Picture books of our gods, for kids: the Navadurga Set is out now at rishikatha.com (link in bio).\n\n💬 GOLD or HEALTH: what are YOU asking for this Dhanteras? Comment below!\n🔖 Save this for Friday and send it to the one who's already planning the jewellery shop trip.\n➡️ Next: do your Diwali aarti WITH our reel. Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it.\n\n#dhanteras #dhanteras2026 #dhanvantari #diwali #diwali2026 #samudramanthan #ayurveda #lakshmi #hindupurana #bhagavatapurana #sanatandharma #hinduism #indianfestivals #yamadeepdaan #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1793539959, "like_count": 3517, "comment_count": 12, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.com/"}, "formats": [{"format_id": "dash-1637191617906417a", "ext": "m4a", "tbr": 53.853, "asr": 48000, "format_note": "DASH audio", "container": "m4a_dash", "vcodec": "none", "acodec": "mp4a.40.5", "url": "https://instagram.fblr22-1.fna.fbcdn.net/o1/v/t2/f2/m78/AQNpPMioNDqnUfIcSSMtV2GWJ